values ('e5f6a7b8-9c0d-4e13-8f23-3a4b5c6d7e53', '19th-and-20th-century-philosophy', '19th and 20th Century Philosophy', 'Core study covers consciousness, history, negation, the master-slave dialectic, and social freedom; historical materialism, the commodity form, exploitation, class struggle, and ideology critique; anxiety, despair, inwardness, faith, indirect communication, and stages of life; perspectivism, morality, ressentiment, genealogy, nihilism, and self-overcoming; meaning, belief, truth, inquiry, habit, experience, and democracy; intentionality, reduction, being-in-the-world, embodiment, and lived experience; freedom, bad faith, absurdity, ambiguity, oppression, and decolonial subjectivity; Frege, Russell, logical analysis, ordinary language, meaning, reference, and truth; reason, domination, the culture industry, ideology, reification, and emancipation; Saussure, Foucault, Derrida, discourse, genealogy, deconstruction, and subject formation; standpoint, embodiment, recognition, coloniality, intersectionality, and epistemic injustice; and how 19th-20th century movements shape current debates in ethics, politics, mind, language, and culture.');

